Subject: [PATCH 2/2] add --connect-timeout for reaching a just-launched server

The evaluator launches CARLA, sleeps 30 s, then tries to connect up to 20
times. Each attempt used the client timeout, which is --timeout (default
600 s). When the server needed more than 30 s to come up, the first attempt
blocked for the full ten minutes before the retry that then connected at once:
"time-out of 600000ms while waiting for the simulator", then "load_world
success, attempts=1". On 2026-10-16 that cost 3 of 10 routes about ten minutes
each.

Lowering --timeout itself is not a fix: the same value bounds `load_world` on
the large towns and the agent and tick watchdogs, where a short limit would
fail routes that are only slow. So the connection attempts get a timeout of
their own, and the client goes back to --timeout once connected. Without the
flag the behaviour is upstream's.

Upstreamable.

diff --git a/leaderboard/leaderboard/leaderboard_evaluator.py b/leaderboard/leaderboard/leaderboard_evaluator.py
index 0958f7d..a2fcf95 100644
--- a/leaderboard/leaderboard/leaderboard_evaluator.py
+++ b/leaderboard/leaderboard/leaderboard_evaluator.py
@@ -213,7 +213,11 @@ class LeaderboardEvaluator(object):
                 client = carla.Client(args.host, args.port)
                 if args.timeout:
                     client_timeout = args.timeout
-                client.set_timeout(client_timeout)
+                # Each connection attempt waits --connect-timeout, then the next
+                # one starts; the server can still be booting after the 30 s
+                # sleep, and a first attempt at the full --timeout (600 s) spent
+                # ten minutes waiting on a server that answered seconds later.
+                client.set_timeout(args.connect_timeout or client_timeout)
 
                 settings = carla.WorldSettings(
                     synchronous_mode = True,
@@ -222,6 +226,7 @@ class LeaderboardEvaluator(object):
                     spectator_as_ego = False
                 )
                 client.get_world().apply_settings(settings)
+                client.set_timeout(client_timeout)
                 print(f"load_world success , attempts={attempts}", flush=True)
                 break
             except Exception as e:
@@ -528,6 +533,9 @@ def main():
                         help='Use CARLA recording feature to create a recording of the scenario')
     parser.add_argument('--timeout', default=600.0, type=float,
                         help='Set the CARLA client timeout value in seconds')
+    parser.add_argument('--connect-timeout', default=None, type=float,
+                        help='Client timeout for each attempt to reach a just-launched server, '
+                             'in seconds (default: --timeout)')
 
     # simulation setup
     parser.add_argument('--routes', required=True,
